BT /F2 22 Tf 72 710.0 Td (Chapter 2: Newton's Laws) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.5 Tf 72 672.3 Td (Isaac Newton explained motion with three laws that connect forces to the way objects) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.5 Tf 72 656.8 Td (move. These laws remain the foundation of engineering, from bridges to rockets.) Tj ET
BT /F2 15 Tf 72 627.3 Td (Force and Inertia) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.5 Tf 72 599.0 Td (A force is a push or a pull that acts on an object. Inertia is the tendency of an object) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.5 Tf 72 583.5 Td (to resist any change in its motion. The first law states that an object stays at rest or) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.5 Tf 72 568.0 Td (keeps moving in a straight line unless an unbalanced force acts on it. Heavier objects) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.5 Tf 72 552.4 Td (have more inertia, which is why a loaded truck is harder to stop than a bicycle.) Tj ET
BT /F2 15 Tf 72 522.9 Td (The Second Law) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.5 Tf 72 494.7 Td (The second law tells us exactly how much an object accelerates. The acceleration depends) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.5 Tf 72 479.1 Td (on the net force and on the mass of the object. A larger force causes a larger) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.5 Tf 72 463.6 Td (acceleration, while a larger mass leads to a smaller one.) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 112 442.1 Td (F = m \327 a) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.5 Tf 72 417.9 Td (For example, pushing a 10 kilogram cart with a force of 20 newtons gives it an) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.5 Tf 72 402.4 Td (acceleration of 2 meters per second squared. Doubling the force doubles the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.5 Tf 72 386.8 Td (acceleration.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.5 Tf 72 363.3 Td (To solve a force problem, follow these steps:) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.5 Tf 86 345.8 Td (1. Draw the object and every force acting on it.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.5 Tf 86 328.3 Td (2. Add the forces to find the net force.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.5 Tf 86 310.7 Td (3. Divide the net force by the mass to get the acceleration.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.5 Tf 86 293.2 Td (4. Check that the direction of your answer makes sense.) Tj ET
BT /F2 15 Tf 72 263.7 Td (Action and Reaction) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.5 Tf 72 235.4 Td (The third law states that every action has an equal and opposite reaction. When a) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.5 Tf 72 219.9 Td (swimmer pushes water backward, the water pushes the swimmer forward. Rockets work the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.5 Tf 72 204.4 Td (same way, because hot gas thrown downward lifts the rocket upward.) Tj ET
endstream
