BT /F2 22 Tf 72 710.0 Td (Chapter 3: Energy) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.5 Tf 72 672.3 Td (Energy is the ability to do work. It is never created or destroyed, but it constantly) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.5 Tf 72 656.8 Td (changes from one form into another. This principle is called the conservation of energy,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.5 Tf 72 641.3 Td (and it is one of the most important ideas in science.) Tj ET
BT /F2 15 Tf 72 611.7 Td (Kinetic and Potential Energy) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.5 Tf 72 583.5 Td (Kinetic energy is the energy an object has because of its motion. Potential energy is) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.5 Tf 72 568.0 Td (the energy stored in an object because of its position. A book on a high shelf has) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.5 Tf 72 552.4 Td (potential energy, which becomes kinetic energy as the book falls.) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 112 530.9 Td (KE = 1/2 m v^2) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 112 508.7 Td (PE = m g h) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.5 Tf 72 484.5 Td (For example, a roller coaster at the top of a hill has mostly potential energy. As it) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.5 Tf 72 469.0 Td (races down, that energy transforms into kinetic energy and the cars reach their highest) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.5 Tf 72 453.5 Td (speed at the bottom.) Tj ET
BT /F2 15 Tf 72 423.9 Td (Summary) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.5 Tf 72 395.7 Td (Motion is described by speed, velocity, and acceleration. Forces cause acceleration, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.5 Tf 72 380.2 Td (the second law links force, mass, and acceleration together. Energy changes form but the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.5 Tf 72 364.6 Td (total amount always stays the same.) Tj ET
endstream
